                                     0000     1 	.TITLE	DBG113	Phase 113 probe: the debugger's open questions
                                     0000     2 	.IDENT	/01/
                                     0000     3 ; DBG113.MAR - the program behind Phase 113's debugger round (README.md). Each
                                     0000     4 ; routine is the stage for one group of questions; the sessions (DBG113*.DBG)
                                     0000     5 ; stop in it. START declares an exit handler (EXIT and QUIT), then calls:
                                     0000     6 ;
                                     0000     7 ;   REC(3)      a recursion to LEAF, as testdata/dbg89's: REC(n) writes
                                     0000     8 ;               n*^X100 + k in Rk (R1 to R5) and saves R2 to R4, not R5, with
                                     0000     9 ;               IV set by its entry mask; LEAF saves R6, not R7, sets DV, and
                                     0000    10 ;               leaves the condition codes N set at INLEAF (the scope round)
                                     0000    11 ;   FLOATS      short literals in F, D, G, and H instructions
                                     0000    12 ;   REGINS      registers holding an instruction's bytes (EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION
                                     0000    13 ;               of a register)
                                     0000    14 ;   LOOP twice  three passes over LOOPTOP each, writing WATCHL and COUNT
                                     0000    15 ;               (tracepoints and watchpoints)
                                     0000    16 ;   SUBA, SUBD, SUBE   each calls one of SUBB1 to SUBB3 (STEP/RETURN and
                                     0000    17 ;               STEP/OVER interrupted by a break)
                                     0000    18 ;   TWICE       a macro: one source line, two calls of SUBC (a line step
                                     0000    19 ;               that ends at a RET in the middle of the caller's line)
                                     0000    20 ;   SIGNAL      two unhandled warnings (exception breaks)
                                     0000    21 ;
                                     0000    22 ; and prints "DBG113: done". The exit handler prints "DBG113: the exit
                                     0000    23 ; handler ran".
                                     0000    24 
